          "label": "DATE",
          "start": 2065,
          "end": 2075
        }
      ],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 18,
      "text": "4. The aforesaid affidavit appears available on  record.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 2079,
      "end": 2135,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 19,
      "text": "5. The petitioners are in-laws.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 2138,
      "end": 2169,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 20,
      "text": "6. In view of submission as the maintenance of  opposite party no. 2 appears settled with her husband against  one time payment for sum of Rs. 08 lacs,",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 2172,
      "end": 2323,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 21,
      "text": "where their  marriage also stands dissolved as per their personal law, and  as such, the dispute appears amicably settled and, therefore,\n in such circumstances continuing with the process against the  petitioners qua in-laws would only amount to an abuse of the  process of the court of law.\n 7.",
      "rhetorical_role": "PREAMBLE",
      "start": 2324,
      "end": 2620,
      "entities": [],
      "in_summary": true,
      "summary_section": "PREAMBLE"
    },
    {
      "sentence_id": 22,
      "text": "In this context, guiding note may be import from  legal report of Hon'ble Supreme Court as available through  Abhisek Vs. State of Madhya Pradesh, reported in 2023  SCC OnLine SC 1083.\n Patna High Court CR.",
      "rhetorical_role": "NONE",
